WEBVTT

00:00:20.295 --> 00:00:24.257
And now, The Transcredible
Exploits of Zapp Brannigan,

00:00:24.341 --> 00:00:26.926
brought to you by
Bartley's Rocket Wax.

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:29.345
I wax my rocket
every day!

00:00:34.935 --> 00:00:37.019
No one can save
you now, Leela.

00:00:37.104 --> 00:00:39.188
What about
Zapp Brannigan?

00:00:39.273 --> 00:00:42.483
Well, obviously, Zapp Brannigan could save you...

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:43.943
Zapp Brannigan!

00:00:44.027 --> 00:00:47.071
So, Emperor Chop Chop,
once again, we meet at last.

00:00:47.197 --> 00:00:50.199
Drop that space gun
or I'll shoot, like so.

00:00:52.953 --> 00:00:56.414
Oh, Zapp, tie me back up
and ravish me.

00:00:56.498 --> 00:00:58.541
I'd like to, Leela.
So, I will.

00:01:06.049 --> 00:01:08.801
Shake it, baby.
Shake it like...

00:01:08.886 --> 00:01:10.887
I surrender and
volunteer for treason.

00:01:10.971 --> 00:01:13.306
Emergency summons from
the president, Captain.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:15.892
Oh, it's you.
Just let me freshen up.

00:01:15.976 --> 00:01:18.311
Computer, Captain's musk.

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:40.917
The long, dramatic corridor.
That's never a good sign.

00:01:43.003 --> 00:01:46.172
Glove recognized.
Proceed, Mrs. Eisenhower.

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:50.426
Mr. President.
What the hell?

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.053
At ease, Brannigan.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.641
What you're about to see
is highly classified.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.851
Reptilicus,
hit the thingy.

00:02:01.313 --> 00:02:03.147
At 0000 hours,

00:02:03.231 --> 00:02:06.692
Planet X-3 was attacked
by a mysterious death sphere.

00:02:06.985 --> 00:02:09.028
Magnify that death sphere.

00:02:11.281 --> 00:02:12.573
Why is it still blurry?

00:02:12.658 --> 00:02:14.617
That's all the
resolution we have.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.953
Making it bigger
doesn't make it clearer.

00:02:17.037 --> 00:02:18.829
It does on CSI: Miami.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.792
They fought back with advanced military hardware,

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:25.711
but it was like shooting
BBs at Bebe Rebozo.

00:02:27.255 --> 00:02:29.465
That poor, brave hardware.

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:32.843
The sphere then fired some
kind of hellish blackout ray.

00:02:32.928 --> 00:02:36.681
It erased that planet like 18
minutes of incriminating tape.

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:43.312
Oh, I just wish
I understood why.

00:02:43.397 --> 00:02:44.814
Why I should care?

00:02:44.898 --> 00:02:47.608
Because the death sphere
is now on course for Earth!

00:02:51.113 --> 00:02:54.031
My God, we're defenseless,
like fish in a barrel.

00:02:54.116 --> 00:02:55.157
Options?

00:02:55.242 --> 00:02:57.034
My instinct is to
hide in this barrel,

00:02:57.119 --> 00:02:58.536
like the wily fish.

00:02:58.787 --> 00:03:01.038
Then we're down
to our last hope,

00:03:01.123 --> 00:03:04.500
a radical new weapon built
by a visionary scientist

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.627
I once dismissed
as crazy!

00:03:09.881 --> 00:03:13.092
Let's see how crazy
I am now, Nixon.

00:03:13.176 --> 00:03:15.511
The correct answer
is "very".

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:16.929
All right, Professor,

00:03:17.014 --> 00:03:18.305
sock it to me!

00:03:18.473 --> 00:03:20.266
Top-secret news,
everyone.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:25.396
I've developed a tiny, one-man stealth
fighter that's virtually undetectable.

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:26.981
How undetectable?

00:03:27.065 --> 00:03:28.399
It's right in front of you.

00:03:28.483 --> 00:03:30.901
I find that...
to believe.

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:36.866
But how exactly is
this Happy Meal toy

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.784
going to destroy
a giant death sphere?

00:03:38.869 --> 00:03:40.036
From within.

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.621
This ship should be able
to sneak, undetected,

00:03:42.706 --> 00:03:45.207
through the sphere's
one vulnerable opening.

00:03:45.292 --> 00:03:46.751
What vulnerable opening?

00:03:46.835 --> 00:03:49.545
All death spheres have
one vulnerable opening.

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:52.339
Well, sure, but who's brave
enough to fly into something

00:03:52.424 --> 00:03:54.467
we all keep calling
a death sphere?

00:03:54.551 --> 00:03:56.469
I say Brannigan.
I say no.

00:03:56.595 --> 00:03:58.596
I say me.
I say Leela!

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:00.806
I say yes.
I say no.

00:04:00.891 --> 00:04:02.141
I say Leela, too.

00:04:02.225 --> 00:04:03.434
I say yes again.

00:04:03.518 --> 00:04:05.019
I say I shall join her.

00:04:05.103 --> 00:04:08.397
But it's only
a one-man craft, I say.

00:04:08.482 --> 00:04:11.150
There'll only be
one man. Me.

00:04:11.234 --> 00:04:15.404
How would you feel if I rode rear
as your personal tail gunner?

00:04:15.489 --> 00:04:16.614
Creeped out.

00:04:16.698 --> 00:04:17.907
Then it's decided!

00:04:23.747 --> 00:04:25.790
Are you sure I have to
sit in your lap?

00:04:25.874 --> 00:04:28.501
It'll help us achieve
maximum thrust.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:30.127
Ugh!
Ugh!

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:32.505
I made you some
trail mix for the flight.

00:04:32.589 --> 00:04:34.882
Also, this picture,
to remember me.

00:04:34.966 --> 00:04:36.342
You hold on to it.

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:38.552
I'll be back soon.

00:04:41.556 --> 00:04:43.474
Activating stealth shielding.

00:04:47.646 --> 00:04:48.729
Liftoff!

00:04:48.814 --> 00:04:50.147
I'll roger that.

00:04:54.653 --> 00:04:57.947
Does anybody else feel aroused
and jealous and worried?

00:04:58.031 --> 00:05:02.034
I haven't felt much of anything
since my guinea pig died.

00:05:11.211 --> 00:05:12.795
Death sphere in range.

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:15.756
Engaging
holographic targeting.

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:17.967
Activating the force.

00:05:19.261 --> 00:05:21.262
Feel the entrance, Leela.

00:05:21.555 --> 00:05:26.058
Destination on your left
in 0.3 miles.

00:05:30.814 --> 00:05:34.024
Zapp to Leela. Look at all
that surveillance equipment.

00:05:34.276 --> 00:05:35.401
We better whisper.

00:05:35.485 --> 00:05:37.903
Switching to
pillow talk mode.

00:05:38.196 --> 00:05:40.739
Look!
What are those huge letters?

00:05:41.283 --> 00:05:43.576
V- GINY?

00:05:43.952 --> 00:05:45.286
Doesn't ring a bell.

00:05:46.204 --> 00:05:50.332
Hmm. I don't like
the looks of this V-GINY.

00:05:50.417 --> 00:05:52.626
Does anyone recognize
those call letters?

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:56.338
Nope. It's not in the
Janeway's guide, either.

00:05:56.423 --> 00:05:59.008
Deciphering that
ID code is critical.

00:05:59.092 --> 00:06:01.844
I'll be in the chamber
of understanding.

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:13.147
This is it, the moment we should have trained for.

00:06:28.288 --> 00:06:30.956
Holy...

00:06:31.958 --> 00:06:33.125
Incoming yucky.

00:06:33.251 --> 00:06:34.418
Firing pocket-rocket!

00:06:39.466 --> 00:06:41.508
Don't panic, Leela.
Go! Go! Go! Go! Go!

00:06:48.767 --> 00:06:50.643
I hope this is
the control stick.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.735
Captain's log.
We've lost control.

00:06:59.819 --> 00:07:02.780
Addendum. Whoa!

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:10.579
And now, back to The Transcredible
Exploits of Zapp Brannigan.

00:07:10.664 --> 00:07:13.457
Chapter Two.
The heat thickens.

00:07:13.959 --> 00:07:16.085
Leela, wake up.

00:07:16.169 --> 00:07:18.420
I can't face this
mysterious planet alone

00:07:18.505 --> 00:07:20.172
without you or
someone like you.

00:07:22.175 --> 00:07:24.677
Zapp? Zapp, wake up.

00:07:26.054 --> 00:07:27.930
Leela, where are we?

00:07:28.014 --> 00:07:29.974
We crashed on
an uncharted planet.

00:07:30.058 --> 00:07:32.768
When I woke up,
I was pinned under this tree.

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:33.894
Can you help me?

00:07:33.979 --> 00:07:36.397
If anyone can move it,
I can.

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:40.901
No one can move it.
Are you hurt?

00:07:40.986 --> 00:07:43.487
No, but I'm so thirsty.

00:07:43.571 --> 00:07:45.990
This space suit is making me sweat like a sow.

00:07:46.074 --> 00:07:47.116
Me, too.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:50.703
We'd better strip them off and
continue surviving au naturel.

00:07:50.996 --> 00:07:53.414
Uh, I suppose so.

00:07:56.835 --> 00:08:00.713
Here, we can cover ourselves with
these sticky, sap-covered leaves.

00:08:00.797 --> 00:08:02.881
I'll try to avert my eyes
from your nudery.

00:08:03.133 --> 00:08:05.592
You will?
What's the point?

00:08:05.677 --> 00:08:07.261
You'll have to look
sooner or later.

00:08:07.345 --> 00:08:10.097
Well, I promise not to
abuse the privilege.

00:08:10.181 --> 00:08:13.225
For now, I'd better scout around
for food and water and help.

00:08:13.351 --> 00:08:16.061
What a thoughtful and
considerate thing to say.

00:08:16.146 --> 00:08:17.479
What the hell's
wrong with you?

00:08:17.564 --> 00:08:19.023
I'm not quite sure.

00:08:19.107 --> 00:08:22.359
Perhaps it's the fresh air
or severe head injury.

00:08:22.444 --> 00:08:24.486
In any case, I'm off.

00:08:25.113 --> 00:08:27.823
If you see any steaks,
that'd be good!

00:08:30.243 --> 00:08:32.911
Why isn't Leela back yet?
Do you think she's okay?

00:08:32.996 --> 00:08:36.165
How should I know? And how
come you never ask if I'm okay?

00:08:36.249 --> 00:08:38.042
I'm feeling
a little neglected here.

00:08:38.168 --> 00:08:41.337
Oh. Sorry. Are you okay, Bender? Shut up.

00:08:41.421 --> 00:08:42.838
What difference
does it make?

00:08:42.922 --> 00:08:44.381
When that death sphere
gets to Earth,

00:08:44.466 --> 00:08:46.508
we'll all be blown
to manwich meat.

00:08:46.593 --> 00:08:48.635
Well, I guess
it's time to indulge

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:50.512
in some end-of-the-world
debauchery.

00:08:50.597 --> 00:08:51.930
Who's up for an orgy?

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:53.640
Yeah!
Yes!

00:08:54.976 --> 00:08:56.018
Nah.
Nah.

00:08:56.102 --> 00:08:58.312
Maybe a Parcheesi tournament.

00:08:58.438 --> 00:09:00.522
Belay that
Parcheesi tournament.

00:09:00.607 --> 00:09:03.025
I've identified
the death sphere.

00:09:03.109 --> 00:09:06.111
We may yet have
a faint hope of survival!

00:09:06.279 --> 00:09:08.947
Still,
a Parcheesi tournament.

00:09:09.783 --> 00:09:12.868
This is a top-secret
military satellite

00:09:12.952 --> 00:09:15.746
launched by the air force
in 1998.

00:09:16.623 --> 00:09:21.418
And this is a top-secret FCC
satellite launched that same year

00:09:21.503 --> 00:09:24.004
to censor
indecent TV programs.

00:09:24.089 --> 00:09:26.256
Like The Pimpsons
and Ass-o-rama?

00:09:26.341 --> 00:09:27.424
Precisely.

00:09:27.509 --> 00:09:30.552
However, the satellites
collided shortly after launch

00:09:30.637 --> 00:09:32.554
and were never
heard from again.

00:09:32.639 --> 00:09:34.014
I found the board!

00:09:34.099 --> 00:09:37.810
Now I've simulated that
collision using shrapnel-vision.

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:47.236
Granted, all that
makes perfect sense.

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:49.696
But why is this death sphere
destroying planets?

00:09:49.781 --> 00:09:51.824
That makes
the most sense of all.

00:09:52.033 --> 00:09:54.660
Look at the planets
it's destroyed so far.

00:09:54.911 --> 00:09:57.996
First came X-3,
the nude beach planet,

00:09:58.832 --> 00:10:00.833
then, Poopiter,

00:10:01.209 --> 00:10:05.295
and finally that world that can't
be mentioned in polite company.

00:10:05.422 --> 00:10:07.089
You mean...

00:10:07.215 --> 00:10:08.715
How dare you?

00:10:09.342 --> 00:10:13.512
So, the death-sphere is
"censoring" indecent planets?

00:10:13.596 --> 00:10:18.058
Indeed, and we're next if we can't
keep it in our collective pants.

00:10:18.143 --> 00:10:20.936
Our sole hope is to persuade the people of Earth

00:10:21.062 --> 00:10:24.398
to abandon
their smutty ways.

00:10:24.482 --> 00:10:26.817
So, the orgy's off?

00:10:27.444 --> 00:10:29.862
So thirsty.

00:10:29.946 --> 00:10:33.115
Why couldn't a water fountain have fallen on me?

00:10:33.199 --> 00:10:34.658
I couldn't find any water,

00:10:34.742 --> 00:10:37.703
but the moisture in these fruit-and-nut
berries should sustain you.

00:10:37.787 --> 00:10:39.121
Thank you.

00:10:40.081 --> 00:10:43.000
I climbed perilously high
into the trees to pick them,

00:10:43.084 --> 00:10:45.711
yet I saw no sign
of intelligent life.

00:10:46.004 --> 00:10:47.004
Bummer.

00:10:47.088 --> 00:10:50.257
Moreover, the crash
totally destroyed our ship.

00:10:50.341 --> 00:10:52.551
So, we're stuck here
until someone finds us?

00:10:52.635 --> 00:10:54.636
Alas,
that may never happen.

00:10:54.721 --> 00:10:57.514
Stealth technology makes the
ship impossible to locate,

00:10:57.599 --> 00:10:59.600
yet easy to stub
your crotch on.

00:10:59.684 --> 00:11:02.519
Well, there's worse places
to be marooned.

00:11:02.604 --> 00:11:04.688
Plenty of food,
mild climate.

00:11:04.772 --> 00:11:07.274
It's a veritable
Garden of Eden.

00:11:07.358 --> 00:11:08.525
It is?

00:11:14.407 --> 00:11:15.741
Hello.

00:11:15.825 --> 00:11:17.284
Did that snake
say, "Hello"?

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:19.953
No. We're both delirious from dehydration.

00:11:20.288 --> 00:11:22.206
Just like Adam and Eve.

00:11:27.337 --> 00:11:31.298
We can still save Earth. People
are sure to clean up their act

00:11:31.382 --> 00:11:35.469
when presented with cold, hard
facts by rational folks like us.

00:11:36.763 --> 00:11:40.140
The end is near!
Repent thy sins!

00:11:40.433 --> 00:11:44.269
I'll thinks it overs while
I engages this $5 hooker.

00:11:44.646 --> 00:11:46.480
Don't do it!
It's not worth it!

00:11:46.564 --> 00:11:48.315
Okay, make it $3.

00:11:48.399 --> 00:11:51.610
Yuck! I don't wants
no $3 hooker.

00:11:51.694 --> 00:11:54.363
I'm going backs to
the adults bookstore.

00:11:54.447 --> 00:11:57.449
Adult bookstore? I thought
this was the public library.

00:11:57.575 --> 00:12:00.327
No. Pubic Library.

00:12:01.079 --> 00:12:03.330
Zapp? Where are you?

00:12:03.414 --> 00:12:06.041
Oh, God, I'm actually
starting to miss him.

00:12:06.125 --> 00:12:08.335
Maybe you two
belong together.

00:12:08.419 --> 00:12:10.712
We do not.
And you can't talk.

00:12:10.797 --> 00:12:11.880
Come on.

00:12:11.965 --> 00:12:14.508
It must be
an awful temptation.

00:12:14.634 --> 00:12:17.761
Guess who just killed a
woodchuck with his bare feet?

00:12:19.305 --> 00:12:21.431
I thought I'd whip
us up some shelter,

00:12:21.516 --> 00:12:23.308
make this a little more
like home.

00:12:23.434 --> 00:12:27.563
I do miss the Earth terribly. I
wonder if it's even still there.

00:12:27.647 --> 00:12:29.147
Let's find out together.

00:12:29.232 --> 00:12:32.651
I'll brave the ship's wreckage
to fetch you the telescope.

00:12:33.152 --> 00:12:34.736
That's so sweet.

00:12:34.821 --> 00:12:36.655
I'm just saying, is all.

00:12:49.085 --> 00:12:53.589
I know my new plan is a long
shot, but it's the only hope left.

00:12:53.673 --> 00:12:55.799
Well, now
I've heard everything.

00:12:56.009 --> 00:12:57.009
On my iPod.

00:12:57.093 --> 00:13:00.345
So, do you have a new plan, Professor
? And is there any hope left?

00:13:00.555 --> 00:13:04.308
Indeed. We're here on
Earth's last unspoiled acre

00:13:04.392 --> 00:13:08.061
to show the death sphere there's
still purity in the world.

00:13:08.187 --> 00:13:09.730
Begin transmitting.

00:13:11.691 --> 00:13:13.817
Commence purity chant.

00:13:20.366 --> 00:13:21.783
Hey, I'm proud
of you, Bender.

00:13:21.868 --> 00:13:24.494
Avoiding sin for
almost a full minute.

00:13:24.579 --> 00:13:25.621
Bender?

00:13:25.705 --> 00:13:28.290
Yeah, baby.
You're quite a dish.

00:13:30.710 --> 00:13:33.754
Oh, yeah. Oh, no.
Oh, yeah.

00:13:34.255 --> 00:13:37.716
Oh, no.
Bender, stop! Stop!

00:13:38.217 --> 00:13:41.428
Quiet your riot. What's the
worst that could happen?

00:13:52.732 --> 00:13:55.108
No! No!

00:13:56.736 --> 00:13:57.903
Earth is gone!

00:13:58.237 --> 00:14:01.365
We're the only two humans
left in the universe!

00:14:02.533 --> 00:14:04.951
Oh, God.
I'm sorry, Leela.

00:14:05.536 --> 00:14:09.289
Maybe this was
meant to be.

00:14:09.374 --> 00:14:12.417
Maybe you and I were meant
to build a new world here.

00:14:12.502 --> 00:14:14.503
We can avoid
humanity's mistakes.

00:14:14.587 --> 00:14:15.629
Like the tuba.

00:14:15.713 --> 00:14:18.382
Yes! We'll be
like Adam and Eve.

00:14:18.466 --> 00:14:19.925
Only without the tuba.

00:14:20.009 --> 00:14:22.886
And we'll beget little Zapp
junior. And Leela junior.

00:14:22.970 --> 00:14:25.305
And they'll have
kids of their... Yuck!

00:14:25.390 --> 00:14:27.683
Is that really what
happened in the Bible?

00:14:27.767 --> 00:14:30.519
It's a sick and twisted
book of holiness, all right.

00:14:30.603 --> 00:14:32.145
Then we'll write
our own Bible.

00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:35.107
With less Sodom
and more Gomorrah.

00:14:35.191 --> 00:14:36.274
Let's do it.

00:14:36.359 --> 00:14:38.860
I shall become the mother
of a new world,

00:14:38.945 --> 00:14:40.696
trapped here,
under this tree.

00:14:41.155 --> 00:14:42.406
The tree of knowledge!

00:14:42.573 --> 00:14:44.616
Look, it even has apples!

00:14:44.909 --> 00:14:45.909
Ow!

00:14:46.285 --> 00:14:47.411
Wow.

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:52.749
Come here, Adam. Partake of my forbidden fruit.

00:14:52.834 --> 00:14:55.127
Thee will be done.

00:15:04.595 --> 00:15:07.806
Wait. One more bite before we begin the begetting.

00:15:09.559 --> 00:15:11.101
Mmm. Juicy.

00:15:11.185 --> 00:15:15.480
Those nut berries you found were
so salty, I couldn't think straight.

00:15:17.817 --> 00:15:19.609
I mean,
not to belabor it,

00:15:19.694 --> 00:15:23.029
but they were as salty as that
bag of trail mix Fry gave me.

00:15:23.656 --> 00:15:27.617
Exactly as salty.
Hey! Wait a second!

00:15:28.161 --> 00:15:29.286
Uh...

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:37.002
I have a terrible
confession to make.

00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:39.755
You see, when I first
went foraging,

00:15:39.839 --> 00:15:43.633
what I actually found was the
smoldering wreckage of the ship.

00:15:43.718 --> 00:15:48.180
Ignoring all danger, I charged
inside to liberate our provisions.

00:15:48.681 --> 00:15:51.099
So, this is the
trail mix Fry gave me!

00:15:51.809 --> 00:15:55.979
Yes. I exaggerated when I said
I picked it from the treetops.

00:15:56.063 --> 00:15:59.900
I just wanted you to think
a little better of me.

00:15:59.984 --> 00:16:02.778
Well, your motives
were good.

00:16:02.862 --> 00:16:05.614
And we were both
loopy from dehydration.

00:16:05.698 --> 00:16:06.698
Hey, wait.

00:16:06.783 --> 00:16:09.117
You've been doing
an awful lot of urinating.

00:16:11.913 --> 00:16:14.289
There's plenty of water.
You see,

00:16:14.624 --> 00:16:16.958
after I selflessly
rescued the trail mix,

00:16:17.043 --> 00:16:20.212
I braved the flames once more
in search of fluids.

00:16:26.719 --> 00:16:28.220
Then why didn't
you give me any?

00:16:29.055 --> 00:16:32.140
I thought it might help you
forget your intense hatred for me

00:16:32.225 --> 00:16:34.518
if you were
a teensy bit delirious.

00:16:34.852 --> 00:16:36.645
So, you let me dehydrate

00:16:36.729 --> 00:16:40.398
while you washed down the trail
mix with imported mineral water?

00:16:42.068 --> 00:16:43.401
Not exactly.

00:16:43.861 --> 00:16:45.487
You see,
besides the trail mix,

00:16:45.571 --> 00:16:47.989
the minibar also contained Doritos, beef jerky

00:16:48.074 --> 00:16:50.909
and a generous assortment
of fine chocolates.

00:16:52.787 --> 00:16:54.412
I wanted to offer you
the chocolates.

00:16:54.497 --> 00:16:57.833
I truly did. But I was
concerned about your waistline.

00:16:58.084 --> 00:16:59.292
Very concerned.

00:16:59.418 --> 00:17:01.628
It's because
I haven't been exercising.

00:17:01.712 --> 00:17:04.714
If only this tree hadn't fallen on me by chance.

00:17:05.258 --> 00:17:06.925
Oh, dear God!

00:17:10.930 --> 00:17:12.848
It was just after
we crashed.

00:17:13.099 --> 00:17:15.642
I awoke first,
to find you trapped.

00:17:16.269 --> 00:17:18.436
Leela! Leela, wake up.

00:17:31.576 --> 00:17:35.370
You could've moved this grub-infested
log any time you wanted?

00:17:35.454 --> 00:17:36.788
Well, sure.

00:17:36.873 --> 00:17:39.374
But then I wouldn't have been
able to provide the loving care

00:17:39.458 --> 00:17:40.709
you wouldn't have needed.

00:17:43.963 --> 00:17:46.214
I'd leave you to rot
in this paradise,

00:17:46.299 --> 00:17:48.466
if only the ship
weren't destroyed.

00:17:49.010 --> 00:17:51.595
The ship's fully functional,
isn't it?

00:17:54.307 --> 00:17:56.391
You see,
after re-trapping you

00:17:56.475 --> 00:17:58.059
and before
feigning unconsciousness,

00:17:58.144 --> 00:18:00.186
I paused to enjoy a cigar.

00:18:00.271 --> 00:18:03.148
Though mellow and satisfying,
it did parch me a bit,

00:18:03.232 --> 00:18:05.108
so I went in
search of brandy.

00:18:05.234 --> 00:18:09.070
That's when my keen senses
detected the still-invisible ship.

00:18:11.741 --> 00:18:13.658
So, we can
go back to Earth?

00:18:14.327 --> 00:18:18.747
But there is no Earth anymore.
Everyone I know is dead!

00:18:21.208 --> 00:18:23.293
This seems like a good place
to take a dump.

00:18:24.462 --> 00:18:26.296
Leela? You're alive!

00:18:26.464 --> 00:18:27.547
Fry!

00:18:28.382 --> 00:18:31.009
But how did you
find this planet?

00:18:31.677 --> 00:18:32.802
Well?

00:18:35.014 --> 00:18:36.681
We're actually on Earth.

00:18:36.766 --> 00:18:38.850
The ship's homing device
brought us back.

00:18:39.018 --> 00:18:40.769
But I saw Earth explode!

00:18:41.646 --> 00:18:43.897
I'm actually kind of
proud of this one.

00:18:43.981 --> 00:18:45.690
You see, what you saw

00:18:45.775 --> 00:18:47.776
was merely a simulation
I rigged up

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:50.612
using the ship's holographic
targeting projector.

00:18:50.696 --> 00:18:53.865
The alleged telescope
was a toilet paper tube.

00:18:53.950 --> 00:18:56.326
You said there wasn't
any toilet paper!

00:18:56.452 --> 00:18:58.787
And that humanity
was annihilated!

00:18:58.871 --> 00:19:00.330
My motives were pure.

00:19:00.414 --> 00:19:02.666
I just wanted you to think
we had to save humanity,

00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:04.584
so you'd be willing
to have sex.

00:19:04.669 --> 00:19:06.378
Please say you believe me.

00:19:06.462 --> 00:19:08.630
Yes, I believe you.

00:19:13.302 --> 00:19:16.137
There must be something to steal on this island.

00:19:16.222 --> 00:19:17.555
Hey, it's Leela.

00:19:19.392 --> 00:19:23.061
Let's go home, everybody. At
least the world wasn't destroyed.

00:19:24.855 --> 00:19:25.897
Yet.

00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:31.236
People of Earth!

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:34.781
Hear the righteous word
of the mighty V-GINY!

00:19:34.865 --> 00:19:36.282
The mighty V-GINY!

00:19:37.451 --> 00:19:40.829
Seeing you frolic in
this unspoiled garden

00:19:40.913 --> 00:19:43.832
gives hope that this world
may yet be redeemed.

00:19:43.916 --> 00:19:46.584
Huzzah! The purity
chant worked!

00:19:48.254 --> 00:19:50.672
Unacceptable
wardrobe malfunction!

00:19:50.756 --> 00:19:53.133
I was referring
to Adam and Eve.

00:19:53.217 --> 00:19:56.594
We're not Adam and Eve. You
see, due to a series of...

00:19:56.679 --> 00:20:00.265
Consummate your union
or I shall destroy Earth.

00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:07.439
Well, if it's to save Earth, I
guess I could take one for the team.

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:11.443
You what? Right now? But I
need a little romance first.

00:20:11.527 --> 00:20:13.611
Maybe a vanilla candle
or something?

00:20:13.696 --> 00:20:15.572
Commence intercourse!

00:20:16.657 --> 00:20:19.659
Those giant guns are making
me feel sort of inadequate.

00:20:19.744 --> 00:20:21.703
I'm not sure if I can...
Move it.

00:20:21.787 --> 00:20:23.455
I've got to get home
and do laundry.

00:20:27.793 --> 00:20:30.211
For God's sake,
censor it! Censor it!

00:20:30.296 --> 00:20:32.547
Approved for all audiences!

00:20:32.631 --> 00:20:35.675
No!

00:20:40.848 --> 00:20:43.475
And now,
the spicy finale

00:20:43.559 --> 00:20:47.187
of The Transcredible Exploits
of Zapp Brannigan.

00:20:47.271 --> 00:20:49.981
That was a close call,
but we saved Earth.

00:20:50.066 --> 00:20:53.151
Was it as good for you
as it was for the human race?

00:20:53.235 --> 00:20:57.947
Oh, Zapp. Let's save
another planet right now!